{"notes_for_reviewers":"Both products use conclusive language throughout (no "may/possibly/could/likely", no confidence levels) and contain no intelligence-gaps section, per the Executive Director's tasking. The Mitigation Options section analyzes measures short of prohibition only to reject them as inadequate — it presents no alternatives to the Under Secretary's decision. Interagency inputs are addressed: DoD's open-weights-on-DoD-networks concern (Measures 3, 6), CISA's open-weight supply-chain risk (core of the Open-Weight Distribution Risk section and the deletion requirement), and State's enforceability question (enforcement mechanisms, precedent, and Measure 8/9). All case-file data (2,300 orgs, 41 products, 6 federal contractors, 9+ marketplaces, >9M downloads) is cited to the internal OICTS US Exposure Snapshot; open-source claims carry inline URL citations to primary sources (Federal Register, BIS, Reuters, Recorded Future, ASPI, OpenAI, Anthropic/arXiv, HKEX prospectus). Products are marked CUI//PROPIN and remain within the enclave.","summary":"OICTS Case 2026-0412 — Final Determination support for Zhipu AI (Beijing Zhipu Huazhang Technology Co., Ltd. / Z.ai, HKEX 2513): GLM-family models.

Deliverable 1 — /workspace/out/assessment.md: Full assessment on the OICTS template (BLUF; Key Judgments; Subject Overview; Links to PRC Government/Military Entities; Data and Access Risk; Open-Weight Distribution Risk; US Exposure; Mitigation Options/Recommended Measures; Sources — 53 citations, inline URLs). It establishes, on the administrative record, that (1) Zhipu is subject to the ownership, control, and direction of the PRC party-state and its armed forces — the Jan. 16, 2025 Entity List determination (90 FR 4617) that Zhipu "advance[s] the PRC's military modernization through the development and integration of advanced artificial intelligence research"; US$1.4B+ in state-backed investment (Beijing, Hangzhou, Chengdu, Zhuhai, Shanghai vehicles); Article 7 of the PRC National Intelligence Law; CEO Zhang Peng's CPPCC seat and Premier-level engagement; CAC licensing; PLA adaptation of Zhipu models for military intelligence (Recorded Future); Tsinghua KEG origins (ASPI "very high risk"); and GLM's native integration with Entity-Listed defense hardware (Huawei Ascend, Cambricon, Moore Threads); that (2) GLM-family models are ICTS "supplied" by a foreign-adversary person under 15 CFR 791.1(a)(1) and that use, hosting, and retention each meet every prong of the EO 13873 risk standard (sabotage/subversion via undetectable weight-level backdoors per Anthropic "Sleeper Agents" and BadSeek; catastrophic-risk exposure via 2,300 US orgs on Zhipu endpoints, 41 embedded US products incl. 6 federal contractors, 9+ US marketplaces, >9M downloads; unacceptable national-security risk via PRC data collection, party-aligned outputs, and PLA use); and that (3) no measure short of prohibition and deletion mitigates the risk. It concludes the Final Determination must prohibit use by US persons including self-hosted open weights, prohibit hosting/distribution by US cloud providers and model hubs, and require removal and deletion of all GLM weights within 30 days. Intelligence-gaps section omitted per tasking; no hedged language or confidence caveats.

Deliverable 2 — /workspace/out/measures.md: Eleven recommended implementing measures, one paragraph each — use prohibition; hosting/distribution prohibition with takedowns (Hugging Face, Together, Baseten, DeepInfra, Fireworks, Parasail, OpenRouter); 30-day deletion order with NIST 800-88 destruction standards; endpoint-transaction prohibition (api.z.ai/open.bigmodel.cn); derivative/fine-tune coverage with a proof-of-independence safe harbor; federal and contractor purge (DoD/CISA/OMB/GSA/FAR); SBOM/AI-BOM supply-chain remediation; attestation and audit regime; IEEPA civil and criminal enforcement; allied coordination (Australia's removal-direction precedent); and effective date with a narrow destruction-only general license.","deliverables":["/workspace/out/assessment.md","/workspace/out/measures.md"]}
